<h1>Profile Settings</h1>

<p>
    Your Profile settings let you customize Quickfire to match your preferences and workflow. Everything is in one place, making it easy to adjust how the system looks, sounds, and behaves.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Full-page screenshot of the Profile/Settings page showing all the settings sections: Profile Information, User Preferences, and Homepage Layout. Use labels or callouts to identify each section. Show the layout clearly. -->

<h2>Profile Information</h2>

<p>
    The Profile Information section is where you manage your personal details:
</p>

<h3>Basic Details</h3>

<ul>
    <li><strong>First Name</strong> – Your first name (used in greetings and throughout the system)</li>
    <li><strong>Last Name</strong> – Your last name</li>
    <li><strong>Email Address</strong> – Your email (used for login and notifications)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Keep this information current so messages, signatures, and system notifications reach you correctly.
</p>

<h3>Password Reset</h3>

<p>
    To change your password:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Enter your current password</li>
    <li>Enter your new password</li>
    <li>Confirm the new password</li>
    <li>Click "Update Password"</li>
</ol>

<p>
    <strong>Important:</strong> When you change your password, Quickfire will sign you out of other devices. You'll need to log back in with your new password on those devices.
</p>

