<h2>User Preferences</h2>

<p>
    User Preferences control how Quickfire looks, sounds, and feels. These are personal settings that don't affect other users.
</p>

<h3>Audio Enabled</h3>

<p>
    This toggle turns sound effects and audio notifications on or off. When enabled, you'll hear:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Sound effects for certain actions</li>
    <li>Audio notifications for important events</li>
    <li>System sounds for feedback</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Turn this off if you prefer a quieter experience or work in a shared space.
</p>

<h3>Spicy Visuals</h3>

<p>
    This controls animations and visual effects throughout Quickfire. When enabled, you'll see:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Smooth transitions and animations</li>
    <li>Visual effects for interactions</li>
    <li>Enhanced visual feedback</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Turn this off if you prefer a simpler, less animated interface or if animations cause performance issues.
</p>

<h3>Safety's On</h3>

<p>
    This enables simplified interface mode, which:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Reduces visual complexity</li>
    <li>Simplifies the interface</li>
    <li>Removes some advanced features for a cleaner experience</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Use this if you want a more streamlined, focused interface with fewer distractions.
</p>

